  ### What mas configure-airgap Does
  Once mas mirror-images finishes, your private registry has all the images, but your OpenShift cluster does not know how to use them yet.
  Running mas configure-airgap:
  1. Configures ImageDigestMirrorSet (IDMS) / ICSP: Tells OpenShift to redirect requests for cp.icr.io, quay.io, and icr.io to your private registry (192.168.2.
  225:32500/jllairgap/...).
  2. Updates the Global Cluster Pull Secret: Injects your registry credentials (jllairgap:jllairgap@2026) into openshift-config/pull-secret so every cluster
  node can authenticate and pull images.
  3. Trusts the Registry CA Certificate: Adds the registry's root CA to OpenShift's trusted CA bundle so nodes trust its TLS certificate.
  ──────
