  ### Step-by-Step Instructions:

  #### Step 1: Wait for mas mirror-images to return to the prompt

  Once the CLI image finishes mirroring, the prompt will return:

    [ibmmas/cli:23.17.1]mascli$

  #### Step 2: Run mas configure-airgap

  In the same container, run:

    mas configure-airgap

  #### Step 3: Provide the following inputs when prompted:

   Prompt                                             │ Recommended Value                                  │ Notes
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Mirror Registry Host                               │ 192.168.2.225                                      │ Node IP of your cluster
   Mirror Registry Port                               │ 32500                                              │ Registry NodePort
   Mirror Registry Prefix                             │ jllairgap                                          │ The repository prefix used during mirror
   Mirror Registry CA File                            │ /mnt/registry/ca.crt                               │ (Already prepared and verified)
   Mirror Registry Username                           │ jllairgap                                          │
   Mirror Registry Password                           │ jllairgap@2026                                     │
   Enable IBM managed Red Hat catalogs?               │ n (or y if you mirrored RH catalogs)               │ Default is n if only MAS was mirrored
   Enable IBM managed Red Hat Release?                │ n                                                  │
  ──────
  ### What Comes After mas configure-airgap?

  After the airgap configuration is applied to OpenShift:

  1. OpenShift will create the ImageDigestMirrorSet resources.
  2. You can proceed with installing the IBM Operator Catalog and the suite using:
    mas install
